# The Charas Ball — nine pinches rolled together.
#
# PLACEHOLDER art. Warlon Mhite may redraw it; that is what the .mctex is for.
#
# ## Why a ball and not a bar
#
# The family lands three colours on three FORMS — a pinch, a brown pressed bar, a blonde pressed bar
# — and a fourth flat slab would collapse that to three colours on two forms. Charas is rubbed off a
# LIVING plant and rolled between the palms; it is never pressed, and the shape it is actually sold
# in (Malana cream, charas sticks) is a ball. So the block is a ball, and it is the one member of
# the family you pull apart by hand instead of cutting.
#
# The palette is item/charas's own, opened up by two steps at the top: a block face is low contrast
# (vanilla blocks span a median 76 luminance steps against an item's 164) but near-black needs a
# little more room than that or the whole thing reads as a hole in the world.
#
# The surface is the tell. Charas is soft, sticky and faintly glossy — hand-rolled resin picks up a
# sheen from the palms — so the highlight is ONE soft cluster up-left rather than a gradient, and the
# grain is irregular rather than granular. It is not powder; it has been worked.

@palette default
. = none
1 = 100C09      the deepest crease
2 = 1A150F
3 = 251E15      the body of the ball
4 = 32291C
5 = 3F3423
6 = 4E402C      lit face
7 = 60503A      the palm sheen; one cluster, up-left, nowhere else

@texture block/charas_ball 16x16 type=block
